<title>MEXICO: Duff &amp; Phelps sees Mexico Q4 GDP growing 4.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Duff &amp; Phelps sees Mexico Q4 GDP growing 4.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 1996 fourth-quarter GDP will be 4.5 percent, Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating estimated on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The positive evolution of the GDP in the third quarter of 1996 (7.4 percent) makes a statement that the strength of the recovery is greater than even the authorities predicted,&quot; Duff &amp; Phelps said in a report.</p>
<p>With 4.5 percent growth in the fourth quarter, Mexico would post an annual growth rate of 4.6 percent, Duff &amp; Phelps said.</p>
<p>For 1997, the rating agency estimated growth at between 4.6 percent and five percent, with inflation of about 18 percent.</p>
<p>The Mexican peso should weaken a little to nearly nine per U.S. dollar by the end of 1997, Duff &amp; Phelps said.</p>
<p>Rates for the benchmark 28-day treasury bills, or Cetes, should average between 22 percent and 24 percent, the agency said.  </p>
